The register restructure is running (one Opus agent). It will:
- collapse the 640 criteria into atomic concepts;
- add the four new row kinds: performance criterion, trigger, defined level and drafting layer;
- apply the sense splits;
- name concepts first met outside English by the instrument's own phrase, with no English gloss;
- seed the equivalence-class skeleton with only forms already evidenced, including your parking, qualifier and lift/elevator examples;
- write a proposed adopting-instrument key in its README, unpopulated.

Output goes to `scratchpad/session_2026-11-06-base-vocabulary-review/register-v2/`.

When it reports, I'll check its counts and spot-check rows, then launch the equivalents wave: 14 pairs, each doing a second reading of the texts already in hand plus the non-instrument sources the synthesis recommended (statutes, then road-sign and signage manuals, then municipal guidance, then disabled people's organisations' guides). That wave writes an `equivalents.tsv` per pair, with no database rows until the tooling PR merges. I'm holding it until the register exists, so the pairs read against the restructured list and not the one the synthesis found defective.

